# From: Wakelin et al. Molecular Simulation, 2005, 31, 315-322,
# http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/08927020500065850:
#
# For molecular or condensed matter simulations this would need to cover
# at least the following information:
# 
#   - Atomic coordinates;
#     _atom_site_fract_[xyz], _atom_site_Cartn_[xyz] (core dic) 
#
#   - Lattice vectors;
#     _cell_length_[abc], _cell_angle_[alpha,beta,gamma] (core dic)
# 
#   - Forcefields, interatomic potentials;
#     This dictionary
# 
#   - Basis sets;
#     DFT dictionary
# 
#   - Methodology (type of calculation, algorithms, etc.);
#     This dictionary
# 
#   - Control parameters (precision, number of iterations, etc.);
#     This dictionary
# 
#   - Job parameters (time, memory, number of processors, etc.)
#     This dictionary, still incomplete.

